{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>For his father and for his mother.</b> And all the more so for his wife and his daughter and for others. And some say that the word נזיר is from the root נזר, and the proof is 'the נזר of his Elohim is upon his head,' and it is not far-fetched. And know that all the children of men are servants of worldly desire, and the true king — who has a נזר and crown of kingship upon his head — is everyone who is free from desire."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:42.923662778Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}